"""Show and change the account's addressbook: the one SylkServer keeps (XCAP) and Sylk Mobile,
sylk-desktop and Blink share, through the WebRTC gateway. It is cached in
~/.sylkclient/addressbook/<account>.json: showing it does not connect, unless there is no
cache yet or -f is given; a change fetches it anew first, then sends the change.

    sylk-addressbook                                  the contacts, then the groups (fetched once, then cached)
    sylk-addressbook -f                               fetched anew
    sylk-addressbook contacts [TEXT]                  the contacts (whose name or address has TEXT)
    sylk-addressbook groups                           the groups and the names of their contacts
    sylk-addressbook policies
    sylk-addressbook show CONTACT|GROUP               everything about one
    sylk-addressbook show -c [CONTACT]                the contacts, or one contact
    sylk-addressbook show -g [GROUP]                  the groups (with their number of contacts), or one group and its contacts
    sylk-addressbook --check                          what Blink (Cocoa, Qt) and Sylk Mobile would repair, and where they disagree

    sylk-addressbook contact add NAME URI [URI...]    URI: user (the account's domain), user@domain, a number,
                                                      or TYPE=URI (mobile=+31612345678)
    sylk-addressbook contact rename CONTACT NAME
    sylk-addressbook contact add-uri CONTACT URI
    sylk-addressbook contact remove-uri CONTACT URI
    sylk-addressbook contact delete CONTACT

    sylk-addressbook group add NAME
    sylk-addressbook group rename GROUP NAME
    sylk-addressbook group add-contact GROUP CONTACT [CONTACT...]
    sylk-addressbook group remove-contact GROUP CONTACT [CONTACT...]
    sylk-addressbook group delete GROUP               (its contacts stay)

CONTACT and GROUP: an id, a name, a unique part of a name, or for a contact one of its addresses
(delete takes no part of a name: the whole name, an address or the id).
The gateway only gives the addressbook to a registered account: it is registered while connected.
"""

